n stdout write error.\n   \n   - **cmd/wc/main.go** (436 lines, needs modification)\n     - R6.2 is PARTIALLY implemented already. `processFiles()` (lines 83-103) handles file errors: prints error to stderr, sets `hadError=true`, uses `continue` to skip to next file. `run()` (lines 43-76) returns 1 if `hadError` is true.\n     - R6.3 is NOT implemented. `printLine()` (lines 315-322) calls `fmt.Fprintln(w, line)` without checking the error return. `printResults()` (lines 226-242) similarly doesn't track write errors.\n     - Key functions: `run()`, `processFiles()`, `printLine()`, `printResults()`, `collectFields()`, `countFile()`\n     - `countFile()` (lines 105-118) wraps file open errors with the path error message\n     - The `run` function signature: `func run(opts options, files []string, stdout io.Writer, stderr io.Writer) int`\n\n   - **cmd/wc/wc_test.go** (652 lines, needs modification)\n     - Has TestDiff (stdin-based tests), TestDiffFiles (file-based tests), TestDiffFiles0Stdin, TestDiffR52\n     - Uses `writeFixture()` helper to create temp files\n     - No existing tests for R6.2 (non-existent file) or R6.3 (stdout write error)\n     - `defaultEnv = []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}`\n     - DiffTest ExitCode field defaults to 0; needs to be set to 1 for error tests\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R6.2 is partially implemented (file error handling exists in processFiles) but needs test coverage\n   - Identified that R6.3 (stdout write error detection) is completely unimplemented - `fmt.Fprintln` return values are ignored\n   - For R6.3 implementation, need to check write errors from `fmt.Fprintln`/`fmt.Fprintf` in `printLine()` and propagate the error status back to `run()` to return exit code 1\n   - For R6.2 testing, can use DiffTest with a non-existent filename and `ExitCode: 1`\n   - For R6.3 testing, this is difficult to test