{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UocYQ4WAMkJBMrwyVtGbvp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n**R6.2 (exit 1 on file errors)** — was already implemented in `processFiles()` but had a bug: when a file failed among multiple files, the total line was suppressed because `shouldShowTotal` used `len(results)` (successfully processed files) instead of the original file count. Fixed by passing `numFiles` (the count of requested files) through `printResults` to `shouldShowTotal`. Added 6 differential tests covering: nonexistent file alone, before/after/between valid files, and with `-l`/`-w` flags.\n\n**R6.3 (exit 1 on stdout write error)** — was unimplemented. `printLine` now returns `error` from `fmt.Fprintln`, and `printResults` tracks write failures and returns a `bool`. `run()` exits 1 if any write error occurred.\n\nFiles modified:\n- `cmd/wc/main.go` — `printLine` returns error, `printResults` returns write-error bool and takes `numFiles`, `run` checks write errors\n- `cmd/wc/wc_test.go` — added `TestDiffR62` with 6 test cases using binary-name and error-case normalizers\n- `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` — R6.2 and R6.3 marked complete with issue 5183"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":54137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e527becd-86c8-4146-8648-fb7cdc0490d0","uuid":"ed6ceca5-0847-4982-9ea4-2b631f4c6df8"}
